    "title": "Michigan basketball vs Arizona recap in Final Four: Wolverines blow out Wildcats",
    "text": "Updated April 4, 2026, 11:45 p.m. ETThe Michigan Wolverines blast the Arizona Wildcats in the Final Four at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.Michigan star Yaxel Lendeborg suffers an ankle and knee injury, leaving his availability for the title game uncertain.The Wolverines play UConn on Monday night for the national championship.The Michigan Wolverines beat the Arizona Wildcats 91-73 in the Final Four at Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.Aday Mara scores 26 points with 9 rebounds, and Trey McKenney adds 16 points off the bench.Yaxel Lendeborg scores 11 points despite suffering ankle and knee injuries in the first half, while Elliot Cadeau has 13 points, 10 assists and 4 steals.The Wolverines play Connecticut, which handled Illinois in Saturday's opener, on Monday night, April 6, for the national championship. Lendeborg's availability could be iffy.Koa Peat scores 16 points with 11 rebounds, Jaden Bradley and Brayden Burries add 13 each, and Motiejus Krivas 11 for Arizona. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan is in controlMichigan 88, Arizona 66, 3:02 left 2H: Michigan has led by 30 points. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Trey McKinney gets in on the act for MichiganMichigan 72, Arizona 45, 12:17 left 2H: Trey McKenney scores 8 points in a hurry and is up to 13. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan's Yaxel Lendeborg returns to gameMichigan 56, Arizona 39, 15:40 left 2H: Despite being hobbled, Yaxel Lendeborg makes a pair of 3-pointers as Michigan extends its lead to 22 points. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan leads Arizona at halftimeMichigan 48, Arizona 32, halftime: Aday Mara has 15 points and 5 rebounds to lead Michigan, which is 5-of-12 on 3-pointers. Elliot Cadeau has 5 points, 6 assists, 4 rebounds and 3 steals. Arizona is shooting 38% from the field. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan leads Arizona despite foul troubleMichigan 35, Arizona 23, 4:27 left 1H: Trey McKenney's 3-pointer extends Michigan's lead. Michigan star Yaxel Lendeborg has a knee issue, as well as a twisted ankle. He is out for at least the rest of the first half.Arizona's Motiejus Krivas and Koa Peat have 6 points each. Jaden Bradley has 3 fouls.Michigan's Morez Johnson Jr. is called for his 2nd foul at the 6:06 mark and Aday Mara is called for his 2nd foul at the 6:56 mark. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan leads ArizonaMichigan 28, Arizona 21, 7:21 left 1H: Arizona's 9-2 run prompts a Michigan timeout. Yaxel Lendeborg tweaks his left ankle and heads to the locker room, but is expected to return.Less than 10 minutes in, Arizona faces a 16-point deficit, its largest this season. The Wildcats, experts at getting to the free throw line, have shot just 4 so far. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan leads ArizonaMichigan 22, Arizona 10, 11:34 left 1H: Michigan is 9-of-18 from the field, Arizona 4-of-12. The Wildcats have committed 6 turnovers. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Aday Mara leads Michigan vs. ArizonaMichigan 16, Arizona 5, 14:27 left 1H: Michigan big man Aday Mara has 6 points. Timeout, Arizona. NCAA Final Four score tonight: Michigan's Yaxel Lendeborg is in foul troubleMichigan 10, Arizona 3, 15:59 left 1H: The Wolverines run to an early 10-1 lead despite star Yaxel Lendeborg committing 2 fouls in a 5-second span. Michigan coach Dusty May takes in the Illinois-UConn game liveBefore coaching his team against Arizona, Michigan's Dusty May gets a feel for his potential opponents.What time does Michigan basketball play Arizona in the Final Four of March Madness on Saturday, April 4? Start time for Michigan-Arizona game in NCAA Tournament on Saturday, April 4The Michigan Wolverines and Arizona Wildcats at approximately 8:54 p.m. ET Saturday, April 4, 2026, in Lucas Oil Stadium in Indianapolis.What channel is the Michigan vs. Arizona game on Saturday, April 4? Where to watch Michigan basketball play Arizona in the Final Four of March Madness on Saturday, April 4The game will air on TBS at 8:54 p.m. ET on Saturday, April 4.Watch NCAA tournament action on SlingHow to stream Michigan-Arizona game Saturday, April 4. Where to watch Arizona-Michigan March Madness 2026 NCAA tournament game liveThe Michigan Wolverines and Arizona Wildcats will stream on SlingTV at 8:54 p.m. ET, Saturday, April 4, 2026. Fans can download SlingTV in the Apple App Store or on Google Play.Watch NCAA tournament action with a free Fubo trial Michigan 2026 NCAA Tournament resultsFirst round: Michigan 101, Howard 80Second round: Michigan 95, Saint Louis 72Sweet 16: Michigan 90, Alabama 77Elite 8: Michigan 95, Tennessee 62Arizona 2026 NCAA Tournament resultsFirst round: Arizona 92, Long Island 58Second round: Arizona 78, Utah State 66Sweet 16: Arizona 109, Arkansas 88Elite 8: Arizona 79, Purdue 64Who are Michigan's best players?Yaxel Lendeborg averages 14.9 points, 7.0 rebounds and shoots 37.4% from 3=-point range.Morez Johnson Jr. averages 13.2 points and 7.3 rebounds.Aday Mara averages 11.9 points, 6.8 rebounds and 2.6 blocked shots.Elliot Cadeau averages 10.3 points and 5.7 assists, making 37.5% of his 3s.Trey McKenney averages 9.7 points, making 38.5% of his 3s.Who are Arizona's best players?Brayden Burries averages 16.1 points with 40.2% 3-point shooting and 4.9 rebounds.Koa Peat averages 14.1 points and 5.5 rebounds. Jaden Bradley averages 13.3 points on 39.4% 3-point shooting and 4.4 assists.Ivan Kharchenkov averages 10.5 points and 4.3 rebounds.Motiejus Krivas averages 10.4 points and 8.2 rebounds.Michigan basketball roster 202642, Will Tschetter0, Ricky Liburd1, Trey McKenney2, L.J. Cason3, Elliot Cadeau4, Nimari Burnett5, Oscar Goodman7, Howard Eisley Jr.10, Winters Grady11, Roddy Gayle Jr.12, Charlie May13, Harrison Hockberg15, Aday Mara21, Morez Johnson Jr.23, Yaxel Lendeborg32, Malick KordelArizona basketball roster 20260, Jaden Bradley2, Dwayne Aristode3, Anthony Dell'Orso5, Brayden Burries6, Bryce James7, Jackson Francois8, Ivan Kharachenkov10, Koa Peat11, Jackson Cook13, Motiejus Krivas15, Sidi Gueye20, Mabil Mawut21, Evan Nelson22, Addison Arnold30, Tobe Awaka42, Sven DjopmoLeBron James' son is on the Arizona rosterBryce James, son of LeBron James, is on the Wildcats roster.Coach Dusty May was a student manager for Bob Knight at IndianaDusty May has Michigan in the Final Four in his second season. He coached Florida Atlantic for six seasons before joining Michigan, leading the Owls to the 2023 Final Four. May grew up in Greene County, Indiana, and was a student manager for Bob Knight's Indiana teams from 1996-2000.Arizona coach Tommy Lloyd is in his fifth seasonTommy Lloyd is in his fifth season as Arizona coach after a long stint as a Gonzaga assistant. He owns a 148-35 record and has made the NCAA Tournament in all five seasons.",
